  Merged into the app manifest by gradle. One addition:

  - REQUEST_INSTALL_PACKAGES: Android 8+ only reaches the package installer's
    consent flow for a calling app that declares it. Declaring it does NOT
    bypass unknown-source restrictions - it is what lets the user grant Fress
    the standard per-app "install unknown apps" toggle that the system
    installer then enforces on every install.

  The plugin deliberately does NOT declare its own FileProvider: the Tauri
  app project already ships one (authority `<applicationId>.fileprovider`,
  exported=false, grantUriPermissions=true) whose paths live in the generated
  `gen/android/app/src/main/res/xml/file_paths.xml`. A second same-named
  provider resource would collide in the manifest merger, and a same-named
  resource file would be silently shadowed by the app module. Instead, the
  plugin's build.rs idempotently adds the `fress_downloads` files-path entry
  to the GENERATED paths file at build time, so the app's own provider covers
  exactly the engine's downloads directory too.
-->
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">

    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.REQUEST_INSTALL_PACKAGES" />

</manifest>
